  "foaf:name": "Ocean Prediction for Costa Rica",
  "sdo:name": "Ocean Prediction for Costa Rica",
  "sdo:description": "The overall objective of OP4CR is to strengthen Costa Rica’s scientific and technical capacities related to the Digital Ocean and Ocean Prediction to sustainably manage a healthy and resilient ocean, based on the best available science and technology. The project aims to enhance Costa Rica’s ability to access, use, and produce its own Ocean Prediction–based digital resources and operational services. To achieve these goals, OP4CR is structured into two phases over two years (January 2025–December 2026). The first six-month phase aims to demonstrate the relevance of Ocean Prediction–based operational services for marine monitoring in the Cocos Island Marine Protected Area by co-designing a tool with national stakeholders. Building on the results of this phase, the second will focus on assessment and planning, including a capacity-building strategy to collect the information needed to develop an action plan for establishing an Ocean Prediction Service Center (OPSC) in the country.",
